      "side": 0,
      "message": "I assume this is what you meant by \"Also cleans up `at()` to not return a reference to a local variable, since I was tired of ClangTidy warning me about it.\".\n\nI\u0027m not sure why it\u0027s saying it returns a ref to a local variable, given that `at()` returns a reference to a member variable. What is the warning exactly? Maybe you can \"fix\" it by assigning the rresult to a local var:\n\n```\nauto\u0026 end_ref \u003d \u0026at(length() - 1);\nend_ptr \u003d \u0026end_ref + 1;\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 448,
        "startChar": 18,
